Manual review corrections for this page's first pass.

- Every vector variable ($\text{a}$, $\text{b}$, $\text{c}$, $\text{i}$,
  $\text{j}$, $\text{u}$, $\text{v}$, and the boat-weight components
  $\text{v}_{1}$, $\text{v}_{2}$) had been converted to upright,
  non-bold \text{} instead of boldface, unlike every other vector-notation
  exercise file in this repo (e.g. vol3-3-2, vol3-3-3, vol3-3-4,
  vol3-4-6, which all use \mathbf{a}, \mathbf{i}, \mathbf{j}, \mathbf{u},
  \mathbf{v}, ...) and unlike OpenStax's own boldface vector convention;
  changed every such occurrence to \mathbf{}.
- The scalar tension magnitudes $\text{T}_{1}$ and $\text{T}_{2}$ (not
  vectors) had been given the same upright \text{} treatment; changed to
  plain italic $T_{1}$, $T_{2}$, matching how other named scalar variables
  are typeset elsewhere in the repo (e.g. $T_{1}$, $T_{2}$, ... in
  vol3-5-7-change-of-variables-in-multiple-integrals.tex).
- "and c = 0 Determine the scalars" left the zero vector $\text{c}$ as
  bare, non-mathematical prose with no sentence-ending punctuation before
  the next sentence; changed to "and $\mathbf{c}=\langle0,0\rangle$.
  Determine the scalars", matching the component-form notation used for
  $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{b}$ earlier in the same sentence.
- "in the direction of vector $PQ$" referred to the vector between named
  points $P$ and $Q$ without the arrow notation ($\overset{\to}{PQ}$)
  this file otherwise uses for such vectors (e.g. items 1-8, and the
  $\overset{\to}{AD}$ item later in this file); changed to
  $\overset{\to}{PQ}$.
- "point $Q(2,z_{0})$ s situated on the line" was missing the "i" of
  "is situated" (the parallel item just above ends "...is situated on
  the line tangent..."); corrected to "is situated".
- "remains constant for any real number $x$" was missing the sentence's
  closing period, unlike the parallel item just above ("...for any real
  number $t$."); added the period.
- "two vectors below the line formina a triangle" had a typo for
  "forming"; corrected.
- "(also abbreviated as $\text{N}43\text{E})$" closed the parenthesis
  inside math mode even though the matching "(" opens in ordinary prose;
  moved the ")" outside the math span, to "$\text{N}43\text{E}$)".

